Your `ReportGenerator.cs` has four categories of static dependencies. Here's the best approach for each, given your `net10.0` target:

---

### 1. File System → `System.IO.Abstractions` (NuGet)

Don't hand-roll a wrapper — use the established package:

```
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

Inject `IFileSystem` — it covers `File.*`, `Directory.*`, and `Path.*` in one interface:

```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem, ...)
{
    fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(path, content);
    fileSystem.Directory.Exists(dir);
    fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(dir);
    fileSystem.Path.Combine(a, b);
}
```

For tests, install the companion package:
```
dotnet add <TestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```
```csharp
var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
mockFs.Directory.CreateDirectory("/tmp/reports");
var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs, ...);
```

---

### 2. Time → Built-in `TimeProvider` (.NET 8+)

No custom wrapper needed. Register the built-in:

```csharp
// Program.cs
builder.Services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System);
```

Inject and use:
```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(..., TimeProvider timeProvider)
{
    var timestamp = timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
}
```

For tests, use `FakeTimeProvider`:
```
dotnet add <TestProject> package Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing
```
```csharp
var fakeTime = new FakeTimeProvider(
    new DateTimeOffset(2026, 7, 19, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
var generator = new ReportGenerator(..., fakeTime);
```

---

### 3. Environment → Custom `IEnvironmentProvider`

No built-in exists — generate a minimal wrapper covering only the two calls you actually use:

```csharp
namespace NeedsWrappers.Abstractions;

/// <summary>
/// Abstraction over System.Environment for testability.
/// </summary>
public interface IEnvironmentProvider
{
    string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable);
    string MachineName { get; }
}
```

```csharp
namespace NeedsWrappers.Abstractions;

/// <summary>
/// Default implementation that delegates to System.Environment.
/// </summary>
public sealed class EnvironmentProvider : IEnvironmentProvider
{
    public string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable)
        => Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(variable);

    public string MachineName => Environment.MachineName;
}
```

Register: `builder.Services.AddSingleton<IEnvironmentProvider, EnvironmentProvider>();`

---

### 4. Console → Custom `IConsole`

Same approach — wrap only `WriteLine`:

```csharp
namespace NeedsWrappers.Abstractions;

public interface IConsole
{
    void WriteLine(string message);
}
```

```csharp
namespace NeedsWrappers.Abstractions;

public sealed class SystemConsole : IConsole
{
    public void WriteLine(string message) => Console.WriteLine(message);
}
```

Register: `builder.Services.AddSingleton<IConsole, SystemConsole>();`

---

